# parseDisplay copies "name", then "type", then "mode" before it ever
# releases any of them. A bad token in "type"'s place throws out of
# copyStringToken() with "name" already on the heap and no parameter list
# involved at all -- a leak shape stringarray.rib (which throws inside
# parseParameterList) does not exercise. gman is expected to fail on this
# file; the point is that it fails without leaking "name".
Display "malformed_out.tif" 5 "rgba"
